I've been playing nethack off and on for a couple of years now, and lurking
in this newsgroup for almost that long, but there is one thing that I am
curious about. I know that save scumming is bad, and posting a YAAP that
was save scummed is even worse. I'm also aware that the player who can post
a YAAP has a great deal of pride in thier accomplishment, and a game that
is scummed doesn't have quite the same feeling of success. But when did
scumming become bad?

Every other type of game allows for scumming, and many times they
encouraged it actively. ("It's a good idea to save before using this item")
I figure that since nethack can trace it's ancestory to pre-internet days,
perhaps there was something in the begining that made scumming bad? Or
maybe I am looking at it from the wrong side. When did save scumming become
accepted for other games?

I'm just curious about the nethack culture versus other games culture. It
is really fascinating looking at how people view games, and how they view
other players and other games. 

